# Object Storage (R2)

## Backend selection

`internal/storage` picks the backend at startup via `storage.Init(cfg)`:

- **R2** when `R2_ACCOUNT_ID`, `R2_BUCKET`, `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, and `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` are all set (S3-compatible API)
- **Local filesystem** otherwise (existing `data/*` and `tmp/` paths)

Use a **separate R2 bucket per environment** (e.g. dev vs prod). Set `R2_BUCKET` in each deployment's `.env`.

## Key layout (R2)

```
avatars/{stored_filename}
teacher-documents/document/{stored_filename}
teacher-documents/resume/{stored_filename}
intro-videos/{stored_filename}
reports/{stored_filename}
backups/{backup_name}.tar.gz
```

## Type-based grouping

When a storage category holds multiple domain types (enum), group objects under `{category}/{type_subdir}/{basename}`.

- Map type to subdir via a method on the domain enum (e.g. `TeacherDocumentType.StorageSubdir()`), not ad-hoc strings in handlers.
- DB continues storing basename only (`stored_filename`); resolve the full storage key at the handler/storage boundary using type + basename (`storage.TeacherDocumentKey`).
- On read/delete, support legacy flat layout fallback during transition (same pattern as reports' `tmp/` fallback).
- New uploads always use the typed subfolder.
- `storage migrate` walks subdirs recursively and uses DB type for legacy flat files.
- `storage reorganize-teacher-documents` moves legacy flat local/R2 objects into typed subfolders without changing the DB.

## DB fields

Continue storing basename only (`stored_filename`, `profile_picture`). Report cache rows store basename in `output_path` going forward; legacy `tmp/...` paths still resolve during transition.

## Handlers

Use `storage.Default()` for Put/Get/Delete/Exists. Teacher documents use `storage.TeacherDocumentKey`, `storage.GetTeacherDocument`, and `storage.DeleteTeacherDocument`. Serve files through existing app routes (`serveStorageObject` in `cmd/storage_http.go`), not public R2 URLs.

## Categories

Typed in `internal/storage/category.go`: `CategoryAvatars`, `CategoryTeacherDocuments`, `CategoryIntroVideos`, `CategoryReports`, `CategoryBackups`.

## Scripts

- `go run . storage migrate`: one-time upload of existing local files to R2 using app credentials from `.env`
- `go run . storage reorganize-teacher-documents`: move legacy flat teacher document files into `document/` and `resume/` subfolders
